    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Weber's least cost theory focuses on determining the optimal location for a manufacturing plant by minimizing transportation, labor, and agglomeration costs. It emphasizes how the weight of inputs and outputs influences location—specifically, whether an industry is weight-reducing (processing raw materials into lighter products) or weight-gaining (adding weight during production). For weight-reducing industries, it's more efficient to locate near raw materials to reduce transportation costs of heavy raw materials.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
