    "prompt": "Please solve the following mathematical problem and provide the final answer.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Simplify\n\\[\\frac{{\\sec x}}{{\\sin x}} - \\frac{{\\sin x}}{{\\cos x}}.\\]\n\nProvide your final answer in \\boxed{{}} format, where the content inside the braces is the exact mathematical expression or number. For example: \\boxed{{42}}. Keep your explanation clear, concise, and within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We start by rewriting the trigonometric functions:  \n$\\sec x = \\frac{1}{\\cos x}$, so the expression becomes:  \n$$\n\\frac{\\frac{1}{\\cos x}}{\\sin x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x} = \\frac{1}{\\sin x \\cos x} - \\frac{\\sin x}{\\cos x}.\n$$\nCombining the terms over a common denominator $\\sin x \\cos x$:  \n$$\n\\frac{1 - \\sin^2 x}{\\sin x \\cos x} = \\frac{\\cos^2 x}{\\sin x \\cos x} = \\frac{\\cos x}{\\sin x} = \\cot x.\n$$\nThus, the simplified expression is $\\boxed{\\cot x}$.",
