      "generated_answer": "It appears there is a formatting issue in the summation expression. The intended sum is likely:\n\n$$\n\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\frac{F_n}{F_{n+1} F_{n+2}},\n$$\n\nwhere $ F_n $ is the $ n $th Fibonacci number, with $ F_0 = 0 $, $ F_1 = 1 $, and so on. Using the identity:\n\n$$\n\\frac{F_n}{F_{n+1} F_{n+2}} = \\frac{1}{F_{n+1}} - \\frac{1}{F_{n+2}},\n$$\n\nwhich can be verified using the Fibonacci recurrence $ F_{n+2} = F_{n+1} + F_n $, the sum telescopes:\n\n$$\n\\sum_{n=1}^\\infty \\left( \\frac{1}{F_{n+1}} - \\frac{1}{F_{n+2}} \\right) = \\frac{1}{F_2} = 1,\n$$\n\nsince $ F_2 = 1 $ and the tail terms cancel out. Thus, the sum converges to:\n\n\\boxed{1}",
