      "generated_answer": "To find the domain of $ f(x) = \\frac{2 - x}{\\log(2 - \\log(x - 2))} $, we must ensure all expressions inside logarithms are defined and denominators are non-zero. First, $ x - 2 > 0 $ so $ x > 2 $. Second, $ \\log(x - 2) $ is defined for $ x > 2 $, and $ 2 - \\log(x - 2) > 0 $ so $ \\log(x - 2) < 2 $, meaning $ x - 2 < 100 $, or $ x < 102 $. Finally, the denominator $ \\log(2 - \\log(x - 2)) \\neq 0 $, so $ 2 - \\log(x - 2) \\ne 1 $, which gives $ \\log(x - 2) \\ne 1 $, so $ x - 2 \\ne 10 $, or $ x \\ne 12 $. Combining these, the domain is $ (2, 12) \\cup (12, 102) $.\n\n\\boxed{(2, 12) \\cup (12, 102)}",
