000000 \\times 2.1605 \\times 10^{-4} = 2 \\times 10^7 \\times 2.1605 \\times 10^{-4} = 2 \\times 2.1605 \\times 10^{3} = 4.321 \\times 10^3 = 4321$\n\nYes, correct.\n\nNow, 0.00021605 is 8 decimal places: positions: 1st: 0, 2nd: 0, 3rd: 0, 4th: 2, 5th: 1, 6th: 6, 7th: 0, 8th: 5\n\nSo digits: 0,0,0,2,1,6,0,5\n\nSum: $0+0+0+2+1+6+0+5 = 14$\n\nBut leading zeros are part of the decimal representation — yes, they are. So we include all digits from decimal point to termination.\n\nSo the sum of the digits is $2 + 1 + 6 + 0 + 5 = 14$? Wait, but there are three leading zeros.\n\n\"All digits in the terminating decimal representation\" — that means all digits that appear after the decimal point until it terminates.\n\nSo the decimal is written as $0.00021605$, so digits are: 0, 0, 0, 2, 1, 6, 0, 5 — that's 8 digits.\n\nTheir sum: 0+0+0+2+1+6+0+5 = 14.\n\nBut let’s confirm the number of decimal places.\n\nSince denominator is $2 \\times 10^7 = 2 \\times 10^7$, so the fraction is $\\frac{4321}{2 \\times 10^7} = \\frac{4321}{2} \\times 10^{-7} = 2160.5 \\times 10^{-7}$\n\nWait, 2160.5 × 10⁻⁷ = 2.1605 × 10³ × 10⁻⁷ = 2.1605 × 10⁻⁴ = 0.00021605 — same.\n\nBut 2160.5 × 10⁻⁷ = 2160.5 divided by 10⁷ = 0.00021605 — yes.\n\nBut 2160.5 × 10⁻⁷ = 21605 × 10⁻⁸ = 21605 / 100000000 = 4321 / 20000000? Let's check.\n\n21605 / 100000000 = 4321 / 20000000? Cross multiply: 21605 × 20000000 = ?\n\nSimpler: 21605 / 10^8 vs 4321 / (2×10^7) = 4321 / 20,000,000 = ?\n\nMultiply numerator and denominator of right side by 5: (4321 × 5) / (100,000,000) = 21605 / 100,000,000\n\nYes! So $\\frac{4321}{20,\\!000,\\!000} = \\frac{21,\\!605}{100,\\!000,\\!000} = 0.00021605$\n\nNow, written out fully: \"0.00021605\" — but as a terminating decimal, it has 8 digits after decimal: 0,0,0,2,1,6,0,5\n\nSo digits: 0,0,0,2,1,6,0,5\n\nSum = 0+0+0+2+1+6+0+5 = 14\n\nTherefore, the sum of the digits is 14.\n\n\\boxed{14}",
