      "generated_answer": "The correct answer is C because water potential (Ψ) is determined by both solute potential (Ψs) and pressure potential (Ψp), expressed as Ψ = Ψs + Ψp. Water moves from areas of higher water potential to lower water potential, not based solely on solute or pressure potential alone. In this case, the 0.5 M solution has a higher water potential than the 0.6 M solution, so water will move out of the dialysis bag.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
