    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We standardize the values 5 and 11 using the z-score formula:  \n$ z = \\frac{X - \\mu}{\\sigma} $.  \nFor $ X = 5 $: $ z = \\frac{5 - 9}{3} = -1.33 $; for $ X = 11 $: $ z = \\frac{11 - 9}{3} = 0.67 $.  \nUsing the standard normal table, $ P(-1.33 < Z < 0.67) = P(Z < 0.67) - P(Z < -1.33) \\approx 0.7486 - 0.0918 = 0.6568 $, which is closest to 0.65361.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
