      "generated_answer": "The all-or-none law applies to individual muscle fibers, meaning each fiber contracts fully or not at all. However, whole muscle force is graded by recruiting more motor units (recruitment) and increasing the frequency of stimulation (rate coding). Thus, the most accurate answer is that force is graded by the number of motor units activated.\n\n\\boxed{H}",
