      "generated_answer": "The duration of a 180° pulse is related to the B₁ field strength by the equation: $ t_{180} = \\frac{\\pi}{\\gamma B_1} $, where $ \\gamma $ is the gyromagnetic ratio of a proton (approximately $ 2.678 \\times 10^8 \\, \\mathrm{rad \\cdot s^{-1} \\cdot T^{-1}} $). Given $ t_{180} = 12.5 \\, \\mu\\mathrm{s} = 1.25 \\times 10^{-5} \\, \\mathrm{s} $, solving for $ B_1 $ yields $ B_1 = \\frac{\\pi}{\\gamma t_{180}} \\approx 9.3 \\times 10^{-4} \\, \\mathrm{T} $.\n\nThus, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{G}",
