      "generated_answer": "The number average degree of polymerization, $X_n$, is defined as the total number of monomer units divided by the total number of polymer chains, which corresponds to $X_n = \\frac{\\sum N_i X_i}{\\sum N_i}$. The weight average, $X_w$, weights each species by its contribution to the total weight, analogous to $M_w$, leading to $X_w = \\frac{\\sum N_i X_i^2}{\\sum N_i X_i}$. This matches option A.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
