    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: An equation of state due to Dieterici is P(V - nb')exp [(na') / (RTV)] = nRT(1) Evaluate the constants a' and b' in terms of the critical constants P_c, V_c, and T_c of a gas.\n\nOptions: \nA. a' = 2RT_cV_c, b' = (V_c / 2)\nB. a' = 2RT_cV_c, b' = V_c\nC. a' = RT_cV_c, b' = (V_c / 3)\nD. a' = 4RT_cV_c, b' = (V_c / 8)\nE. a' = RT_cV_c / P_c, b' = V_c / P_c\nF. a' = (RT_cV_c) / 2, b' = 2V_c\nG. a' = (RT_cV_c) / 4, b' = 3V_c\nH. a' = P_cV_c^2 / T_c, b' = (V_c / P_c)\nI. a' = 3RT_cV_c, b' = (V_c / 4)\nJ. a' = RT_cV_c, b' = V_c\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
