      "generated_answer": "We analyze the limit:  \n$\\lim_{x \\to 0} (\\csc(x) - \\cot(x)) = \\lim_{x \\to 0} \\left(\\frac{1}{\\sin(x)} - \\frac{\\cos(x)}{\\sin(x)}\\right) = \\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{1 - \\cos(x)}{\\sin(x)}$.  \n\nUsing the known limits $\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{1 - \\cos(x)}{x^2} = \\frac{1}{2}$ and $\\lim_{x \\to 0} \\frac{\\sin(x)}{x} = 1$, we rewrite:  \n$\\frac{1 - \\cos(x)}{\\sin(x)} = \\frac{1 - \\cos(x)}{x} \\cdot \\frac{x}{\\sin(x)} \\to 0 \\cdot 1 = 0$ as $x \\to 0$.  \n\nThus, the limit is 0.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
