      "generated_answer": "The process $ S_n $ is a biased random walk on the integers with drift $ E[X_i] = 1 \\cdot 0.8 + (-1) \\cdot 0.2 = 0.6 $. Due to the positive drift, the walk tends to move to the right linearly, and the number of distinct values visited (the range $ R_n $) grows linearly with $ n $. The limit $ \\lim_{n \\to \\infty} \\frac{E[R_n]}{n} $ equals the speed of the walk, which for such a skip-free random walk is $ |E[X_i]| = 0.6 $.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
