      "generated_answer": "We are given that $ x - 3 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{7} $ and $ y + 3 \\equiv 0 \\pmod{7} $, so $ x \\equiv 3 \\pmod{7} $ and $ y \\equiv -3 \\equiv 4 \\pmod{7} $.  \nThen compute $ x^2 + xy + y^2 + n \\pmod{7} $:  \n$ x^2 \\equiv 3^2 = 9 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{7} $,  \n$ y^2 \\equiv 4^2 = 16 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{7} $,  \n$ xy \\equiv 3 \\cdot 4 = 12 \\equiv 5 \\pmod{7} $,  \nSo $ x^2 + xy + y^2 \\equiv 2 + 5 + 2 = 9 \\equiv 2 \\pmod{7} $.  \nThus, we need $ 2 + n \\equiv 0 \\pmod{7} $, so $ n \\equiv 5 \\pmod{7} $. The smallest positive such $ n $ is 5.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
