    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We are to count palindromes of length 2 or more that contain the letter **M**, using **any subset** of the letters from **MISSISSIPPI**. The available letters are: M (1), I (4), S (4), P (2). Since a palindrome requires symmetric letter placement, and we must include **M**, the letter M must be in the center (for odd-length palindromes), because we only have one M. For even-length palindromes, M cannot appear unless we have two Ms, which we don’t — so **M can only appear in odd-length palindromes, at the center**.\n\nWe then count all possible palindromic arrangements (length ≥ 2) containing M by considering symmetric pairs (from I, S, P) on both sides and placing M in the center. After checking all valid combinations (including length 3, 5, 7, 9, 11), the correct total number of such palindromes is **86**.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
