      "generated_answer": "A Type I error occurs when we reject a true null hypothesis (false alarm), while a Type II error occurs when we fail to reject a false null hypothesis (missed detection). In the dialysis center, a Type II error (failing to recalibrate faulty equipment) is more serious because it could endanger patients’ lives. For the towel manufacturer, a Type II error (continuing production of defective towels) is also more serious than unnecessarily halting production (Type I), though less critical than in healthcare.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
