    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To seat 4 boys and 4 girls alternately in a row, we can start with either a boy or a girl. If we start with a boy, the arrangement is B-G-B-G-B-G-B-G; if we start with a girl, it's G-B-G-B-G-B-G-B. For each pattern, the boys can be arranged in 4! ways and the girls in 4! ways. So total arrangements = 2 × 4! × 4! = 2 × 24 × 24 = 1152. However, this is not among the options, so the correct answer must be E.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
