    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The number of internal diagonals in a polygon with $n$ sides is given by the formula $\\frac{n(n-3)}{2}$. For a pentagon ($n = 5$), this becomes $\\frac{5(5-3)}{2} = \\frac{5 \\times 2}{2} = 5$. Therefore, the pentagon has 5 internal diagonals.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
