      "generated_answer": "The total length of Miller Street is 4.5 kilometers, which is 4,500 meters. It is intersected every 250 meters, so the number of intervals is $ 4500 \\div 250 = 18 $. Since the numbering starts at 1st Street (after the first 250 meters), the highest-numbered street is the 18th intersection before Turner Street.\n\nThus, the highest-numbered street is 18th Street.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
