      "generated_answer": "Oak Street runs 2 kilometers (2000 meters) east from Pine Street to Maple Street. It is intersected every 400 meters, so there are 2000 ÷ 400 = 5 intervals. These intersections occur at 400m, 800m, 1200m, 1600m, and 2000m, but Maple Street is not numbered—only the streets in between are numbered starting from 1st Street. Thus, the five intersections include Pine Street (start), then 1st through 4th Streets, and finally Maple Street (end). But since 2000m is the end at Maple Street and not a numbered street, the last numbered street is at 1600m, which is the 4th street.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
