      "generated_answer": "Let the son's current age be $ x $. According to the statement, the father was as old as the son is now at the time of the son's birth. So, the father's age at the son's birth was $ x $, and since the father is now 40, the son's current age is $ 40 - x = x $, which gives $ 2x = 40 $, so $ x = 20 $. Therefore, the son's age 5 years back was $ 20 - 5 = 15 $.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
