    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: a businessman earns $ 26800 in december , thus decreasing his average annual ( january to december ) earnings by $ 1200 . his average annual earnings would be source : cmat preparation\n\nOptions: \nA. $ 29000\nB. $ 33500\nC. $ 40000\nD. $ 41000\nE. $ 42300\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let his average annual earnings before December be $ x $. After earning $26,800 in December, the average decreases by $1,200, so the new average is $ x - 1,200 $. The total earnings for 12 months is $ 12(x - 1,200) $, and this equals the sum of 11 months' earnings ($ 11x $) plus December's earnings ($26,800):\n\n$ 12(x - 1,200) = 11x + 26,800 $  \nSolving: $ 12x - 14,400 = 11x + 26,800 $ → $ x = 41,200 $\n\nSo, the new average (which is asked) is $ x - 1,200 = 40,000 $\n\n\\boxed{C}",
      "success": true,
