    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "When two dice are thrown, there are $6 \\times 6 = 36$ possible outcomes. The number of outcomes where the sum is greater than 7 (i.e., 8, 9, 10, 11, or 12) is 15:  \n- Sum of 8: 5 ways  \n- Sum of 9: 4 ways  \n- Sum of 10: 3 ways  \n- Sum of 11: 2 ways  \n- Sum of 12: 1 way  \nTotal favorable = 5 + 4 + 3 + 2 + 1 = 15.  \n\nSo, the probability is $ \\frac{15}{36} = \\frac{5}{12} $.  \n\n\\boxed{C}",
