      "generated_answer": "The probability of *not* lassoing a cow in one throw is $ 1 - \\frac{1}{3} = \\frac{2}{3} $. The probability of failing all 3 attempts is $ \\left(\\frac{2}{3}\\right)^3 = \\frac{8}{27} $. Therefore, the probability of succeeding at least once is $ 1 - \\frac{8}{27} = \\frac{19}{27} $.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
