      "generated_answer": "The original train has 12 bogies, each 15 meters long, so the total length is $12 \\times 15 = 180$ meters. It crosses a telegraph post in 18 seconds, so the speed of the train is $\\frac{180}{18} = 10$ m/s. After detaching 2 bogies, the new length is $10 \\times 15 = 150$ meters. At the same speed, the time to cross the post is $\\frac{150}{10} = 15$ seconds.\n\nThus, the correct answer is choice C.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
