    "global index": "MathQA_2386",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: the population of a town increased from 50000 to 80000 in a decade . the average percent increase of population per year is :\n\nOptions: \nA. 4.37 %\nB. 5 %\nC. 6 %\nD. 8.75 %\nE. none of these\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the average percent increase per year, we use the formula for compound annual growth rate (CAGR):  \n$$\n\\text{CAGR} = \\left( \\left( \\frac{\\text{Final Population}}{\\text{Initial Population}} \\right)^{\\frac{1}{n}} - 1 \\right) \\times 00\n$$\nHere, the population grows from 50,000 to 80,000 in 10 years:\n$$\n\\text{CAGR} = \\left( \\left( \\frac{80000}{50000} \\right)^{1/10} - 1 \\right) \\times 100 = (1.6^{0.1} - 1) \\times 100 \\approx (1.0481 - 1) \\times 100 = 4.81\\%\n$$\nThis is closest to 5%, so the best choice is:\n\n\\boxed{B}",
      "success": true,
