    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: the average expenditure of a labourer for 10 months was 85 and he fell into debt . in the next 4 months by reducing his monthly expenses to 60 he not only cleared off his debt but also saved 30 . his monthly income is\n\nOptions: \nA. 180\nB. 100\nC. 112\nD. 110\nE. none of the above\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The total expenditure for 10 months is $ 10 \\times 85 = 850 $.  \nIn the next 4 months, he spent $ 4 \\times 60 = 240 $ and saved 30, so he earned $ 240 + 30 = 270 $ in those 4 months.  \nHis total income over 14 months is $ 850 - d + 270 $, where $ d $ is debt, but since he cleared debt and saved 30, income must cover total expenses and add 30. So total income = $ 850 + 240 - d + d + 30 = 1120 $? Wait:\n\nLet his monthly income be $ x $.  \nTotal income in 14 months = $ 14x $.  \nTotal expenditure = $ 10 \\times 85 + 4 \\times 60 = 850 + 240 = 1090 $.  \nHe saved 30, so income = expenditure - debt + savings → but he cleared debt and saved 30.\n\nLet debt = $ 10x - 850 $ (since he spent 850 but income was 10x).  \nThen in next 4 months, income = $ 4x $, expenditure = 240, and he used the surplus to clear debt and save 30.  \nSo: $ 4x - 240 = \\text{debt} + 30 = (10x - 850) + 30 $  \n$ 4x - 240 = 10x - 820 $  \n$ -6x = -580 $ → $ x = 580 / 6 \\approx 96.67 $\n\nBut that’s not in options. Wait:  \nEquation: $ 4x - 240 = (850 - 10x) $ is debt? No: if expenditure > income, debt = 850 - 10x? No — if income is x per month, then debt after 10 months = $ 850 - 10x $? No: if he spent 85 per month, but income is x, then if x < 85, debt = 10(85 - x)? Wait: expenditure = 85, but income = x, so if x < 85, deficit = 10(85 - x)\n\nBut he fell into debt: so total deficit = $ 10 \\times 85 - 10x = 850 - 10x $\n\nThen in next 4 months, he spent 60 per month, income 4x, so surplus = $ 4x - 240 $\n\nThis surplus cleared the debt and saved 30:  \n$ 4x - 240 = (850 - 10x) + 30 $  \n$ 4x - 240 = 880 - 10x $  \n$ 14x = 1120 $ → $ x = 80 $\n\nBut 80 not in options? Wait: 14x = 1120 → x = 80\n\nBut then check: income 80, spent 85 for 10 months → debt = 5×10 = 50  \nNext 4 months: income 4×80 = 320, spent 240, surplus 80 → clears 50 debt and saves 30 → yes! So income is 80\n\nBut 80 is not in options: A.180 B.100 C.112 D.110 E. none\n\nSo correct answer is E.\n\n\\