  {
    "global index": "MathQA_2482",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: what is the range of all the roots of | x ^ 2 - 3 | = x ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 4\nB. 3\nC. 2\nD. 1\nE. 0\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We solve $|x^2 - 3| = x$. Since the right side is $x$, we know $x \\geq 0$ (absolute value is non-negative). Consider two cases:  \n1) $x^2 - 3 = x$ → $x^2 - x - 3 = 0$ → $x = \\frac{1 \\pm \\sqrt{13}}{2}$. Only $\\frac{1 + \\sqrt{13}}{2} \\approx 2.3$ is valid (positive).  \n2) $-(x^2 - 3) = x$ → $-x^2 + 3 = x$ → $x^2 + x - 3 = 0$ → $x = \\frac{-1 \\pm \\sqrt{13}}{2}$. Only $\\frac{-1 + \\sqrt{13}}{2} \\approx 1.3$ is valid.  \n\nThe roots are approximately $2.3$ and $1.3$, so the range (difference between largest and smallest root) is about $1$. The exact difference is $\\frac{1 + \\sqrt{13}}{2} - \\frac{-1 + \\sqrt{13}}{2} = \\frac{2}{2} = 1$.  \n\nThus, the range of the roots is 1.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 112,
        "output_tokens": 298,
        "total_tokens": 410
