  {
    "global index": "MathQA_436",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: a 12 meter long wire is cut into two pieces . if the longer piece is then used to form a perimeter of a square , what is the probability that the area of the square will be more than 4 if the original wire was cut at an arbitrary point ?\n\nOptions: \nA. 1 / 6\nB. 2 / 3\nC. 3 / 10\nD. 1 / 3\nE. 2 / 5\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "Let the wire be cut at a point $ x $ meters from one end, where $ 0 < x < 12 $. Without loss of generality, assume $ x \\leq 6 $, so the longer piece is $ 12 - x $. This longer piece forms the perimeter of a square, so each side is $ \\frac{12 - x}{4} $, and the area is $ \\left( \\frac{12 - x}{4} \\right)^2 = \\frac{(12 - x)^2}{16} $. We want this area > 4:\n\n$$\n\\frac{(12 - x)^2}{16} > 4 \\Rightarrow (12 - x)^2 > 64 \\Rightarrow |12 - x| > 8\n$$\n\nSince $ x \\leq 6 $, $ 12 - x > 8 \\Rightarrow x < 4 $. So for $ x < 4 $, the area > 4. But since the cut is arbitrary, we consider symmetry: the longer piece is always $ \\max(x, 12 - x) $, so the condition $ \\max(x, 12 - x) > 8 $ yields $ x < 4 $ or $ x > 8 $. This interval has length $ 4 + 4 = 8 $, so probability is $ \\frac{8}{12} = \\frac{2}{3} $.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 162,
        "output_tokens": 317,
        "total_tokens": 479
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
      "error": null
