      "generated_answer": "Let the cut be made at a point $ x $ meters from one end, where $ 0 < x < 14 $. Without loss of generality, the longer piece is $ \\max(x, 14 - x) $, so it must be at least 7 meters. The longer piece forms the perimeter of a square, so the side length is $ \\frac{\\text{longer piece}}{4} $, and the area is $ \\left(\\frac{\\text{longer piece}}{4}\\right)^2 $. We want the area $ > 4 $, so $ \\left(\\frac{L}{4}\\right)^2 > 4 \\Rightarrow L > 8 $. Thus, the longer piece must exceed 8 meters. This occurs when $ x < 6 $ or $ x > 8 $. The total favorable length is $ 6 + 6 = 12 $, out of 14, but we must exclude the interval $ [6,8] $ of length 2. So probability is $ \\frac{12}{14} = \\frac{6}{7} $.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
