      "generated_answer": "A 5 cm cube has a surface area of $ 6 \\times 5^2 = 150 \\, \\text{cm}^2 $.  \nWhen cut into 1 cm cubes, there are $ 5^3 = 125 $ small cubes, each with surface area $ 6 \\times 1^2 = 6 \\, \\text{cm}^2 $, so total surface area is $ 125 \\times 6 = 750 \\, \\text{cm}^2 $.  \nThe percentage increase is $ \\frac{750 - 150}{150} \\times 100 = 400\\% $.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
