      "generated_answer": "We are to find the probability that **at least one** of the events A, B, or C occurs when a card is drawn from a standard 52-card deck.\n\nInstead of computing the union directly, it's easier to use the complement: find the probability that **none** of the events occur and subtract from 1.\n\n- Not A: card is **not a heart** → 39 cards (the other three suits)\n- Not B: card **is a face card** → 12 face cards (J, Q, K in 4 suits)\n- Not C: card’s number is **not divisible by 3** and not face card or ace. But Not B ∩ Not C must consider face cards (which have no \"number\"), so we need to find cards that are **not hearts**, **are face cards or number not divisible by 3**, but we want the intersection of “not A”, “not B”, and “not C”? Wait — we want the complement of (A ∪ B ∪ C), which is (not A) ∩ (not B) ∩ (not C).\n\nLet’s proceed carefully.\n\nWe want:\n\nP(A ∪ B ∪ C) = 1 – P(not A ∩ not B ∩ not C)\n\nSo find cards that are:\n- Not a heart (13 × 3 = 39 cards)\n- **Are** a face card (since not B = \"is a face card\") → 12 total face cards (3 per suit: J, Q, K)\n- And the number is **not** divisible by 3 → but face cards don’t have \"numbers\", so for them \"divisible by 3\" doesn’t apply? But the event C is: \"the number of spots (if any) is divisible by 3\" → so if there is no number (i.e., face card), then C does not occur. So for face cards, C is **false** (since no number), so not C is **true** for face cards.\n\nSo let's define:\n- Event C: card has a number (2–10) and that number is divisible by 3 → numbers divisible by 3: 3, 6, 9 → so 3 values\n  → For each suit: 3 number cards (3,6,9) that satisfy C\n  → So per suit: 3 × 4 = 12 cards satisfy C\n\nSo Not C: all cards that either are face cards, or aces, or numbered not divisible by 3 (i.e., 2,4,5,7,8,10)\n\nBack to: P(not A ∩ not B ∩ not C) = cards that are:\n- Not a heart → in clubs, diamonds, spades\n- Face card (not B) → must be a face card\n- Not C → since face cards have no number, they satisfy not C automatically\n\nSo not A ∩ not B ∩ not C = face cards that are **not hearts** → the face cards in clubs, diamonds, spades\n\nEach suit has 3 face cards → 3 suits × 3 = 9 cards\n\nSo P(not A ∩ not B ∩ not C) = 9/52\n\nThen P(A ∪ B ∪ C) = 1 – 9/52 = 43/52\n\nAnswer: \\boxed{F}",
      "success": true,
