    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The given function $ f(x) = \\frac{1}{\\pi(1 + x^2)} $ is the density of the standard Cauchy distribution. We are to find the density of $ Y = X^2 $. Using the transformation method, for $ y > 0 $, the density $ h(y) $ is obtained by:\n\n$$\nh(y) = f(\\sqrt{y}) \\left| \\frac{d}{dy}\\sqrt{y} \\right| + f(-\\sqrt{y}) \\left| \\frac{d}{dy}(-\\sqrt{y}) \\right| = 2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{\\pi(1 + y)} \\cdot \\frac{1}{2\\sqrt{y}} = \\frac{1}{\\pi \\sqrt{y} (1 + y)}\n$$\n\nThis matches option G (after correcting syntax: \"$\\surdy$\" likely means $\\sqrt{y}$). Thus, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{G}",
