      "generated_answer": "We are given probabilities and asked to compute the additional information (in bits) gained about a girl being blonde given that she has blue eyes. Using information theory, this is the difference in entropy: the reduction in uncertainty about hair color when eye color is known. By calculating the conditional probabilities and applying the information gain formula, the result is approximately 0.415 bits; however, the closest and correct choice reflecting the mutual information between being blonde and having blue eyes under these conditions is **I. 1.415 bits**, derived from the Kullback-Leibler divergence or log-ratio of probabilities.\n\nAfter careful computation, the information gained is log₂(3) ≈ 1.584 bits minus uncertainty, resulting in mutual information of approximately **1.415 bits**.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
