    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The output signal-to-noise ratio (SNR) in FM is related to the input SNR and modulation index β by the formula:  \n$$(S_o/N_o) = (3/2) \\beta^2 (S_i/N_i)$$ in linear terms, or approximately in dB:  \n$$ (S_o/N_o)_{dB} \\approx (S_i/N_i)_{dB} + 10 \\log_{10}(3/2) + 20 \\log_{10}(\\beta) $$  \nGiven $ (S_i/N_i) = 40 $ dB, and using this formula:  \nFor β = 5: $ 40 + 1.76 + 20\\log_{10}(5) ≈ 40 + 1.76 + 14 = 55.76 $ dB ≈ 55.7 dB  \nFor β = 10: $ 40 + 1.76 + 20\\log_{10}(10) = 40 + 1.76 + 20 = 61.76 $ dB ≈ 61.7 dB  \nFor β = 105: $ 40 + 1.76 + 20\\log_{10}(105) ≈ 40 + 1.76 + 40.43 = 82.19 $ dB ≈ 82.185 dB  \n\nThese match option B.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
