    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Determine the inverse Laplace transform of F(s), where F(s) is given by F(s) = [(3s + 1) / {{(s - 1)(s^2 + 1)}}]\n\nOptions: \nA. 3e^t + sin t - cos t\nB. e^t - cos t + sin t\nC. e^t - sin t - cos t\nD. e^t + cos t - 2 sin t\nE. 3e^t - cos t - 2 sin t\nF. 2e^t + sin t + 2 cos t\nG. 2e^t - 2 cos t + sin t\nH. 2e^t - 2 sin t + cos t\nI. e^t - 2 cos t + 2 sin t\nJ. 2e^t + 2 cos t - sin t\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We begin by performing partial fraction decomposition on $ F(s) = \\frac{3s + 1}{(s - 1)(s^2 + 1)} $. Assume:  \n$$\n\\frac{3s + 1}{(s - 1)(s^2 + 1)} = \\frac{A}{s - 1} + \\frac{Bs + C}{s^2 + 1}\n$$\nMultiplying both sides by the denominator gives:  \n$$\n3s + 1 = A(s^2 + 1) + (Bs + C)(s - 1)\n$$\nExpanding and equating coefficients:  \nSet $ s = 1 $: $ 3(1) + 1 = 4 = A(1 + 1) \\Rightarrow A = 2 $.  \nNow substitute $ A = 2 $:  \n$$\n3s + 1 = 2(s^2 + 1) + (Bs + C)(s - 1) = 2s^2 + 2 + Bs^2 - Bs + Cs - C\n$$\n$$\n= (2 + B)s^2 + (-B + C)s + (2 - C)\n$$\nMatch with $ 0s^2 + 3s + 1 $:  \n- $ 2 + B = 0 \\Rightarrow B = -2 $  \n- $ -B + C = 3 \\Rightarrow 2 + C = 3 \\Rightarrow C = 1 $  \n- $ 2 - C = 1 $ ✓  \n\nSo:  \n$$\nF(s) = \\frac{2}{s - 1} + \\frac{-2s + 1}{s^2 + 1} = \\frac{2}{s - 1} - 2\\frac{s}{s^2 + 1} + \\frac{1}{s^2 + 1}\n$$\nNow take inverse Laplace transforms:  \n- $ \\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{\\frac{2}{s - 1}\\right\\} = 2e^t $  \n- $ \\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{\\frac{s}{s^2 + 1}\\right\\} = \\cos t $  \n- $ \\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{\\frac{1}{s^2 + 1}\\right\\} = \\sin t $  \n\nSo:  \n$$\nf(t) = 2e^t - 2\\cos t + \\sin t\n$$\n\nThis matches option **G**.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
