    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We start by factoring the denominator:  \n$s^2 + 3s + 2 = (s + 1)(s + 2)$.  \n\nWe express $F(s) = \\frac{8s + 2}{(s + 1)(s + 2)} = \\frac{A}{s + 1} + \\frac{B}{s + 2}$.  \nMultiplying both sides by $(s + 1)(s + 2)$:  \n$8s + 2 = A(s + 2) + B(s + 1)$.  \n\nSet $s = -1$:  \n$8(-1) + 2 = A(1) \\Rightarrow -6 = A$.  \n\nSet $s = -2$:  \n$8(-2) + 2 = B(-1) \\Rightarrow -14 = -B \\Rightarrow B = 14$.  \n\nThus, $F(s) = \\frac{-6}{s + 1} + \\frac{14}{s + 2}$, which matches option H.  \n\n\\boxed{H}",
