    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Evaluate f(t) if F(s) = [(2s^2 + 13s + 17) / {{(s + 1)(s + 3)}}]\n\nOptions: \nA. 2\\delta(t) + (3e^-t + e^-3t)u(t)\nB. 2\\delta(t) + (3e^-t + 2e^-3t)u(t)\nC. 3\\delta(t) + (3e^-t + 2e^-3t)u(t)\nD. 2 + (3e^-t + 2e^-3t)u(t)\nE. 2 + (5e^-t + 2e^-3t)\nF. 2\\delta(t) + (3e^-t + 2e^-3t)\nG. (3e^-t + 2e^-3t)u(t)\nH. 2\\delta(t) + (3e^-2t + 2e^-3t)u(t)\nI. 2\\delta(t) + (4e^-t + 3e^-3t)u(t)\nJ. 2\\delta(t) + (5e^-t + 2e^-3t)u(t)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We are given $ F(s) = \\frac{2s^2 + 13s + 17}{(s + 1)(s + 3)} $. Note that the degree of the numerator is equal to the degree of the denominator, so we must perform polynomial division first. Dividing:\n\n$$\n\\frac{2s^2 + 13s + 17}{(s + 1)(s + 3)} = \\frac{2s^2 + 13s + 17}{s^2 + 4s + 3}\n$$\n\nPolynomial division gives:\n\n$$\n2 + \\frac{5s + 11}{s^2 + 4s + 3} = 2 + \\frac{A}{s+1} + \\frac{B}{s+3}\n$$\n\nSolving: $ 5s + 11 = A(s+3) + B(s+1) $\n\nSet $ s = -1 $: $ 5(-1) + 11 = A(2) \\Rightarrow 6 = 2A \\Rightarrow A = 3 $\n\nSet $ s = -3 $: $ 5(-3) + 11 = B(-2) \\Rightarrow -4 = -2B \\Rightarrow B = 2 $\n\nSo: $ F(s) = 2 + \\frac{3}{s+1} + \\frac{2}{s+3} $\n\nThe inverse Laplace transform of 2 is $ 2\\delta(t) $, and the rest gives $ (3e^{-t} + 2e^{-3t})u(t) $\n\nThus: $ f(t) = 2\\delta(t) + (3e^{-t} + 2e^{-3t})u(t) $\n\nThis matches option **B**.\n\n\\boxed{B}",
      "success": true,
