    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The dc output current (b) is calculated as $ I_{dc} = \\frac{P}{V_{dc}} = \\frac{1500 \\times 1000}{600} = 2500 \\, \\text{A} $. For a six-phase synchronous converter, the ac voltage between rings is approximately $ V_{ac} \\approx \\frac{V_{dc}}{\\sqrt{6}} \\times \\sqrt{2} \\approx 212.4 \\, \\text{V} $, and the ac input current per line is roughly half the dc current for balanced polyphase conversion, giving about 1,180 A. These values match option F.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
