    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10017",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Raise thephasor(8.66 + j5.0) to the second power; to the fifth power.\n\nOptions: \nA. 85\\angle75° and 85,000\\angle170°\nB. 125\\angle55° and 125,000\\angle175°\nC. 80\\angle90° and 500,000\\angle180°\nD. 95\\angle65° and 95,000\\angle165°\nE. 90\\angle70° and 90,000\\angle160°\nF. 75\\angle80° and 75,000\\angle200°\nG. 70\\angle85° and 70,000\\angle190°\nH. 150\\angle45° and 150,000\\angle225°\nI. 110\\angle50° and 110,000\\angle140°\nJ. 100\\angle60° and 100,000\\angle150°\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "First, convert the complex number $ 8.66 + j5.0 $ to polar form. The magnitude is $ \\sqrt{8.66^2 + 5.0^2} \\approx \\sqrt{75 + 25} = \\sqrt{100} = 10 $, and the angle is $ \\tan^{-1}(5.0/8.66) \\approx 30^\\circ $. So, the phasor is $ 10\\angle30^\\circ $. Raising to the second power: $ (10\\angle30^\\circ)^2 = 100\\angle60^\\circ $, and to the fifth power: $ (10\\angle30^\\circ)^5 = 100,000\\angle150^\\circ $, which matches option J.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
