      "generated_answer": "The mean-square quantization error for a uniform quantizer with error uniformly distributed between -S/2 and +S/2 is given by the variance of a uniform distribution over that interval. The variance (or mean-square error) of a uniform distribution on [-a, a] is (a²)/3, and here a = S/2, so the error is (S/2)² / 3 = S²/12.\n\nThus, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}",
