    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10617",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Evaluate the inverse Laplace transform of F(s) if F(s) = [(2s + 4) / (s^2 + 2s + 5)]. Write a generalized Laplace transform pair which can be added to a transform table to transform func-tions of this type.\n\nOptions: \nA. f(t) = 2e^-tcos2t + e^-t sin 3t\nB. f(t) = e^-tcos2t + 2e^-t sin 2t\nC. f(t) = 3e^-tcos2t + 2e^-t sin 2t\nD. f(t) = 2e^-tcos2t - e^-t sin 2t\nE. f(t) = 3e^-tcos2t - e^-t sin 2t\nF. f(t) = 2e^-tcos2t\nG. f(t) = 2e^-tcos3t + e^-t sin 3t\nH. f(t) = e^-tcos3t + 2e^-t sin 3t\nI. f(t) = 2e^-tcos2t + e^-t sin 2t\nJ. f(t) = 2e^-tsin2t + e^-t cos 2t\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We start by rewriting $ F(s) = \\frac{2s + 4}{s^2 + 2s + 5} $. Complete the square in the denominator:  \n$ s^2 + 2s + 5 = (s+1)^2 + 4 $. Then rewrite the numerator in terms of $ s+1 $:  \n$ 2s + 4 = 2(s+1) + 2 $. So,  \n$$\nF(s) = \\frac{2(s+1) + 2}{(s+1)^2 + 2^2} = 2\\frac{s+1}{(s+1)^2 + 4} + \\frac{2}{(s+1)^2 + 4}\n$$\nUsing Laplace transform tables:\n$$\n\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{ \\frac{s-a}{(s-a)^2 + b^2} \\right\\} = e^{at}\\cos(bt), \\quad\n\\mathcal{L}^{-1}\\left\\{ \\frac{b}{(s-a)^2 + b^2} \\right\\} = e^{at}\\sin(bt)\n$$\nHere, $ a = -1 $, $ b = 2 $, so:\n$$\nf(t) = 2e^{-t}\\cos(2t) + e^{-t}\\sin(2t)\n$$\nThis matches option I.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
