      "generated_answer": "We compute the probability by integrating the joint density function over the given region:\n\nPr[0 < X < 3/4, 1/3 < Y < 2] = ∫ₐᵇ ∫ₐᵇ f(x,y) dy dx = ∫₀^(3/4) ∫_(1/3)^1 6x²y dy dx,  \n\nsince f(x,y) = 0 for y > 1. First, integrate with respect to y: ∫_(1/3)^1 6x²y dy = 6x² [y²/2] from 1/3 to 1 = 6x² (1/2 - 1/18) = 6x² (4/9) = (24/9)x² = (8/3)x². Then integrate with respect to x: ∫₀^(3/4) (8/3)x² dx = (8/3)[x³/3]₀^(3/4) = (8/3)(27/192) = (8×27)/(3×192) = 216/576 = 3/8.\n\nThus, the answer is:\n\n\\boxed{H}",
