    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To find the theoretical variance, first compute the mean:  \n$ E[X] = 0 \\cdot \\frac{1}{4} + 1 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} + 2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{8} + 3 \\cdot \\frac{1}{8} = 0 + 0.5 + 0.25 + 0.375 = 1.125 $.  \nThen compute $ E[X^2] = 0^2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{4} + 1^2 \\cdot \\frac{1}{2} + 4 \\cdot \\frac{1}{8} + 9 \\cdot \\frac{1}{8} = 0 + 0.5 + 0.5 + 1.125 = 2.125 $.  \nVariance = $ E[X^2] - (E[X])^2 = 2.125 - (1.125)^2 = 2.125 - 1.265625 = 0.859375 \\approx 0.859 $.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
