    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10741",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A step up chopper has input voltage 110 V and output voltage 150 V. The value of duty cycle is\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.90.\nB. 0.38.\nC. 0.55.\nD. 0.27.\nE. 0.75.\nF. 0.50.\nG. 0.32.\nH. 0.45.\nI. 0.82.\nJ. 0.67.\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "For a step-up chopper, the output voltage is related to the input voltage by the formula:  \n$$ V_o = \\frac{V_{in}}{1 - D} $$  \nwhere $ D $ is the duty cycle. Substituting $ V_o = 150 $ V and $ V_{in} = 110 $ V:\n\n$$ 150 = \\frac{110}{1 - D} \\Rightarrow 1 - D = \\frac{110}{150} = 0.7333 \\Rightarrow D = 1 - 0.7333 = 0.2667 \\approx 0.27 $$\n\nThus, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}",
