    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10421",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find f(t) {{_\\ast}} g(t), where f(t) = t and g(t) = t^2, and the asterisk indicates convolution.\n\nOptions: \nA. (2t^4 / 3)\nB. (t^4 / 12)\nC. (t^5 / 20)\nD. t^3\nE. (t^4 / 4)\nF. (t^2)\nG. (t^4 / 2)\nH. (t^3 / 3)\nI. (3t^4 / 4)\nJ. (t^5 / 5)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The convolution of $ f(t) = t $ and $ g(t) = t^2 $ is defined as:\n\n$$\n(f \\ast g)(t) = \\int_0^t f(\\tau)g(t - \\tau) \\, d\\tau = \\int_0^t \\tau (t - \\tau)^2 \\, d\\tau\n$$\n\nExpanding and integrating:\n$$\n\\int_0^t \\tau (t^2 - 2t\\tau + \\tau^2) \\, d\\tau = \\int_0^t (t^2\\tau - 2t\\tau^2 + \\tau^3) \\, d\\tau = \\left[ \\frac{t^2\\tau^2}{2} - \\frac{2t\\tau^3}{3} + \\frac{\\tau^4}{4} \\right]_0^t = \\frac{t^4}{2} - \\frac{2t^4}{3} + \\frac{t^4}{4}\n$$\n\nCombining terms:\n$$\nt^4\\left( \\frac{1}{2} - \\frac{2}{3} + \\frac{1}{4} \\right) = t^4\\left( \\frac{6 - 8 + 3}{12} \\right) = \\frac{t^4}{12}\n$$\n\nThus, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{B}",
      "success": true,
