      "generated_answer": "The time scale for dynamic similarity in gravity-fed flows is governed by the Froude number, leading to a time ratio proportional to the square root of the length scale ratio: $ t_m / t_p = \\sqrt{\\lambda} $, where $ \\lambda = 1/100 $. Thus, $ t_p = t_m / \\sqrt{\\lambda} = 0.8 / (1/10) = 8 $ min. The mass flow rate ratio is $ \\dot{m}_m / \\dot{m}_p = \\lambda^{5/2} $, so the correct ratio is $ \\lambda^{5/2} $.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
