    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The transfer function of an RC low-pass filter is given as H(f) = [1 / {{1 +jf/f_c}}] wheref_cis the 3-dB frequency. If the input to this filter is a white noise, find the output noise power N_0 of the filter.\n\nOptions: \nA. \\((\\eta f_c\\pi) / 8\\)\nB. \\(5(\\eta f_c\\pi) / 2\\)\nC. (\\etaf_c\\pi) / 3\nD. \\(\\eta f_c\\)\nE. (\\etaf_c\\pi) / 2\nF. (\\etaf_c\\pi) / 4\nG. \\(3(\\eta f_c\\pi) / 4\\)\nH. \\(4(\\eta f_c\\pi)\\)\nI. 2(\\etaf_c\\pi)\nJ. \\(\\eta f_c / \\pi\\)\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The output noise power of an RC low-pass filter with white noise input is obtained by integrating the power spectral density of the input multiplied by the squared magnitude of the frequency response over all frequencies. For a white noise with power spectral density $\\eta/2$, and transfer function $H(f) = 1 / (1 + jf/f_c)$, the output noise power is $N_0 = \\int_{-\\infty}^{\\infty} \\frac{\\eta}{2} |H(f)|^2 df = \\eta f_c \\pi / 2$. This matches option E.\n\n\\boxed{E}",
