    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We compute the partial derivatives of the vector function $ \\mathbf{a}(u, v) = (u^2v, u + e^v, u + v^2) $.\n\n1) $ \\frac{\\partial \\mathbf{a}}{\\partial u} = (2uv, 1, 1) $,  \n2) $ \\frac{\\partial \\mathbf{a}}{\\partial v} = (u^2, e^v, 2v) $,  \n3) $ \\frac{\\partial^2 \\mathbf{a}}{\\partial u \\partial v} = \\frac{\\partial}{\\partial v} \\left( \\frac{\\partial \\mathbf{a}}{\\partial u} \\right) = (2u, 0, 0) $.\n\nThus, the correct answer is **H**.  \n\\boxed{H}",
