      "generated_answer": "The given system is a linear time-invariant system described by the differential equation \\( \\dot{X} = A X + b u \\), with initial condition \\( X(0) = X_0 \\), and an impulse input \\( u(t) = \\delta(t) \\). Given the matrices and vectors:  \n\\( A = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 & 0 \\\\ -2 & 2 \\end{bmatrix} \\), \\( b = \\begin{bmatrix} 1 \\\\ 0 \\end{bmatrix} \\), \\( X_0 = \\begin{bmatrix} -1 \\\\ 0 \\end{bmatrix} \\), and \\( u(t) = \\delta(t) \\), the solution at \\( t = 0^+ \\) (just after the impulse) involves updating the state by the impulse response: \\( X(0^+) = X(0) + b \\cdot 1 = \\begin{bmatrix} -1 \\\\ 0 \\end{bmatrix} + \\begin{bmatrix} 1 \\\\ 0 \\end{bmatrix} = \\begin{bmatrix} 0 \\\\ 0 \\end{bmatrix} \\).  \nHowever, the question likely asks for a component of the state or a derived scalar; given the context and options, the most plausible answer based on the initial state is the first component, which is \\( -1 \\).\n\n\\boxed{J}",
