    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10642",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: The total normalized power of a periodic signal is given by S = ^n=+\\infty\\sum_n=-\\inftyV_nV_n\\textasteriskcentered where V_n= [1 / (\\vertn\\vert)]e-jarctan(n/2)forn = \\pm 1, \\pm 2,... Calculate the ratio: [{{normalized power(second harmonic)}} / {{normalized power (first harmonic)}}].\n\nOptions: \nA. 0.125\nB. 1.5\nC. 0.75\nD. 0.5\nE. 2\nF. 4\nG. 0.6\nH. 1\nI. 0.25\nJ. 3\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The normalized power of the $n$-th harmonic is proportional to $|V_n|^2$. Given $V_n = \\frac{1}{|n|} e^{-j \\arctan(n/2)}$, we have $|V_n| = \\frac{1}{|n|}$, so $|V_n|^2 = \\frac{1}{n^2}$. The ratio of the second harmonic power to the first is $\\frac{|V_2|^2}{|V_1|^2} = \\frac{1/4}{1/1} = 0.25$.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
