    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A negative point charge of 10^-6 coulomb is situated in air at theorigin of a rectangular coordinate system. A second negativepoint charge of 10^-4 coulomb is situated on the positivex axis at a distance of 50 cm from the origin. Whatis theforce on the second charge?\n\nOptions: \nA. 3.6newtons\nB. 3.2 newtons\nC. 1.2 newtons\nD. 1.6newtons\nE. 2.0 newtons\nF. 4.0 newtons\nG. 0.36 newtons\nH. 5.6 newtons\nI. 4.6newtons\nJ. 2.6newtons\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "We use Coulomb's law: $ F = \\frac{k |q_1 q_2|}{r^2} $, where $ k = 9 \\times 10^9 \\, \\text{N·m}^2/\\text{C}^2 $, $ q_1 = 10^{-6} \\, \\text{C} $, $ q_2 = 10^{-4} \\, \\text{C} $, and $ r = 0.5 \\, \\text{m} $.  \nPlugging in: $ F = \\frac{(9 \\times 10^9)(10^{-6})(10^{-4})}{(0.5)^2} = \\frac{0.9}{0.25} = 3.6 \\, \\text{N} $.  \nSince both charges are negative, the force is repulsive, acting along the positive x-axis on the second charge.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
