      "generated_answer": "We are given $ V_{ab}(s) = \\frac{3V(s) + 3s + 27}{s^2 + 6s + 8} $ and $ v(t) = 16e^{-3t}u(t) $, so $ V(s) = \\frac{16}{s+3} $. Substituting:  \n$ V_{ab}(s) = \\frac{3\\cdot\\frac{16}{s+3} + 3s + 27}{(s+2)(s+4)} = \\frac{\\frac{48}{s+3} + 3s + 27}{(s+2)(s+4)} $.  \nCombining terms and performing partial fraction decomposition yields the time-domain response $ v_{ab}(t) = -48e^{-3t} + \\frac{69}{2}e^{-2t} + \\frac{33}{2}e^{-4t} $, which matches option **J**.\n\n\\boxed{J}",
