      "generated_answer": "The short-circuit test data allows us to find the equivalent resistance and reactance. Using the formula for voltage regulation: %Reg ≈ (I Req × cosφ + I Xeq × sinφ) / Vrated × 100, where cosφ = 0.8 (lagging), and computing Req = 214 / (6.25)² ≈ 5.47 Ω, Z = 131 / 6.25 = 20.96 Ω, Xeq = √(Z² − Req²) ≈ 19.8 Ω, we get %Reg ≈ 4.26%.\n\nThus, the correct answer is:\n\n\\boxed{D}",
