    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_10537",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: Find the energy stored in an inductor from t = 0 to t = 1 whose \\textphi -icharacteristic is given by \\textphi (t) = 1/3i^3 (t) and the current through it is given by i (t) = 2 sin t.\n\nOptions: \nA. 1.00 J\nB. 0.75 J\nC. 1.50 J\nD. 4.00 J\nE. 2.50 J\nF. 3.00 J\nG. 1.25 J\nH. 2.75 J\nI. 2.00 J\nJ. 3.50 J\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The flux linkage is given by $\\phi(t) = \\frac{1}{3}i^3(t)$, and the current is $i(t) = 2\\sin t$. However, the energy stored in an inductor is generally $W = \\int_0^t i(t')v(t')\\,dt'$, where $v(t) = \\frac{d\\phi}{dt}$. Since $\\phi = \\frac{1}{3}i^3$, then $v = \\frac{d\\phi}{dt} = i^2 \\frac{di}{dt}$. Substituting $i(t) = 2\\sin t$, we get $v(t) = (2\\sin t)^2 \\cdot (2\\cos t) = 8\\sin^2 t \\cos t$. Then power $p(t) = i(t)v(t) = (2\\sin t)(8\\sin^2 t \\cos t) = 16\\sin^3 t \\cos t$. Integrating from 0 to 1:\n\n$$\nW = \\int_0^1 16\\sin^3 t \\cos t\\, dt\n$$\n\nLet $u = \\sin t$, $du = \\cos t\\,dt$, so when $t = 0$, $u = 0$; $t = 1$, $u = \\sin 1$. Then:\n\n$$\nW = 16 \\int_0^{\\sin 1} u^3 du = 16 \\cdot \\frac{u^4}{4} \\Big|_0^{\\sin 1} = 4\\sin^4(1)\n$$\n\n$\\sin(1) \\approx \\sin(57.3^\\circ) \\approx 0.8415$, so $\\sin^4(1) \\approx (0.8415)^4 \\approx 0.500$, and $4 \\cdot 0.500 = 2.00\\, \\text{J}$.\n\n\\boxed{I}",
      "success": true,
      "token_usage": {
        "input_tokens": 221,
        "output_tokens": 445,
        "total_tokens": 666
      },
      "provider": "openrouter",
