    "global index": "MMLUPro_engineering_9999",
    "prompt": "Please read the following multiple-choice questions and provide the most likely correct answer based on the options given.\n\nContext: None\n\nQuestion: A model of a proposed low-speed crop-dusting plane is to be tested in a wind tunnel capable of maintaining velocities of 264 ft/s, using atmospheric air. The prototype plane has a design wing span of 27 ft and a proposed speed of 88 ft/s. In order to preserve dynamic similarity, what should be the wing span of the model if the wind tunnel is to operate at full speed? Assume the air at these low velocities to be essentially incompressible. In addition, assume that the temperature of atmospheric air and the temperature of the wind-tunnel air are the same.\n\nOptions: \nA. 9 ft\nB. 30 ft\nC. 3 ft\nD. 6 ft\nE. 15 ft\nF. 21 ft\nG. 12 ft\nH. 18 ft\nI. 24 ft\nJ. 27 ft\n\n\nProvide the correct letter choice in \\boxed{X}, where X is the correct letter choice. Keep the explanation or feedback within 3 sentences.",
    "prediction": "qwen/qwen3-235b-a22b-2507",
    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To preserve dynamic similarity, the Reynolds number must be the same for the model and the prototype. Since the air density and viscosity are the same (same temperature and incompressible flow), and the wind tunnel speed is 264 ft/s (3 times the prototype speed of 88 ft/s), the model’s wing span must be scaled inversely to maintain equal Reynolds numbers. Thus, the model wing span should be $ 27 \\, \\text{ft} / 3 = 9 \\, \\text{ft} $.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
