    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "The synchronous speed of an 8-pole, 60 Hz motor is $ N_s = \\frac{120 \\times 60}{8} = 900 $ rpm. The motor stalls at 650 rpm, so the breakdown slip is $ s_b = \\frac{900 - 650}{900} = 0.278 $. This matches the first value in option G, and the rotor frequency at max torque is $ f_r = s_b \\times f = 0.278 \\times 60 \\approx 16.7 $ Hz, confirming consistency.\n\nThe locked-rotor reactance is calculated using $ X_{lr} = \\frac{R_r}{s_b} = \\frac{0.3}{0.278} \\approx 1.08 \\, \\Omega $, which further confirms option G.\n\n\\boxed{G}",
