      "generated_answer": "The RMS value is 30 A, so the peak current is $ I_0 = 30 \\times \\sqrt{2} \\approx 42.4 $ A. The frequency is 25 cycles/sec, so angular frequency $ \\omega = 2\\pi f = 2\\pi \\times 25 = 157 $ rad/s. Since the wave crosses zero in the positive direction at $ t = 0 $, it must be a sine wave: $ i = 42.4 \\sin(157t) $. At $ t = 0.005 $, $ i = 42.4 \\sin(157 \\times 0.005) = 42.4 \\sin(0.785) \\approx 42.4 \\times 0.707 \\approx 30 $ A. The fraction of a cycle is $ 25 \\times 0.005 = 0.125 = 1/8 $.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
