      "generated_answer": "To find the frequency of AABBCC offspring from a cross between two AaBbCc individuals, consider that each gene pair segregates independently. For each locus, the chance of getting a homozygous dominant (e.g., AA) is 1/4, so for three loci: (1/4) × (1/4) × (1/4) = 1/64. Therefore, the frequency of AABBCC is 1/64.\n\n\\boxed{F}",
