    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To calculate sensitivity, we need to know the true positives (men with prostate cancer and a positive test) and the total number of actual cases of disease (all men with prostate cancer, regardless of test result). Sensitivity = True Positives / (True Positives + False Negatives), where false negatives are men with prostate cancer but a negative test (PSA ≤ 5 ng/mL). Therefore, we need the number of men with prostate cancer who had PSA levels ≤ 5 ng/mL, which requires biopsies in those with test results below or equal to 5 ng/mL.\n\n\\boxed{D}",
