    "generated_result": {
      "generated_answer": "To calculate the 90% confidence interval for the mean, we use the formula: CI = mean ± (z × SEM), where SEM = SD / √n and z ≈ 1.645 for 90% confidence. Here, SEM = 25 / √100 = 2.5, so margin of error = 1.645 × 2.5 ≈ 4.1. Thus, the 90% CI is 85 ± 4.1 → approximately 80.9 to 89.1, which rounds to 81–89.\n\n\\boxed{A}",
