      "generated_answer": "The Nernst potential for an ion can be calculated using the formula: $ E = \\frac{61}{z} \\log\\left(\\frac{[\\text{ion}]_{\\text{out}}}{[\\text{ion}]_{\\text{in}}}\\right) $, where $ z $ is the charge of the ion. For a negative ion (anion), $ z = -1 $, and the concentration ratio is $ \\frac{100}{10} = 10 $. Therefore, $ E = \\frac{61}{-1} \\log(10) = -61 \\, \\text{mV} $.\n\n\\boxed{C}",
