      "generated_answer": "Claire feels constant pressure from her friends to maintain her image as a popular, pristine \"princess.\" This includes expectations about her appearance, behavior, and even her virginity. The pressure contributes to her internal conflict and sense of identity, which she begins to question during detention.\n\n\\boxed{{Claire is pressured by her friends to maintain a perfect, popular image, including preserving her virginity and conforming to social expectations, which causes her emotional distress.}}",
      "success": true,
